<title>ITALY: Turkish freighter sinks off Italy, six missing.</title>
<headline>Turkish freighter sinks off Italy, six missing.</headline>
<dateline>PALERMO, Sicily 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Turkish freighter sank in the Mediterranean Sea off the Italian island of Sicily on Wednesday and six of the 11 crew members were missing, port officials said.</p>
<p>They said the ship &quot;Onurk&quot; sank in waters between the western Sicilian town of Trapani and the port of Cagliari on the island of Sardinia about 3 a.m. local (0200 GMT).</p>
<p>Boats sent by the Sicilian port of Palermo rescued five crew members and efforts to find the other six were continuing, the officials said.</p>
